  "flags": {
    "seattle-by-night": {
      "origen": "escena",
      "escena": "larchmont-planta",
      "id": "LUG-11",
      "plano": "larchmont-planta",
      "provisional": false,
      "nota": "<p><strong>Location:</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.Oiln4o98kvxKbOvS]{The Larchmont Building}<br><strong>Scenes:</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.FttkHsYSSaCpIugu.JournalEntryPage.9fTKL8Oeq36BCfU9]{A2-E05 · The Ashes of the Larchmont}</p>\n<p><strong>Arrival (A2-E05, optional scene).</strong> “Four stories of blackened brick, glassless windows, a construction fence with a demolition notice nobody ever acted on.” The fence runs along the sidewalk (railings: you can see through it, you can&#39;t pass) and has a loose panel where you get in. The notice isn&#39;t painted on the map (it has text): the Storyteller describes it. <strong>The flowers:</strong> seven faded plastic ones tied on with wire, and an eighth, new, real, still beaded with water: tile <code>tile-flores-valla</code> on the fence.</p>\n<p><strong>Inside.</strong> Everything is burned: the doors no longer exist (openings), the windows have no glass (openings in the wall). The hallway ends in the collapse from the floors above; 1B and 1C have caved in (mounds of rubble: no way in). Scene with <strong>rain weather</strong>: the roof is gone, and the rain “comes in through the roof and runs down the stairwell to the basement, where you can hear water running.”</p>\n<p><strong>The stairs.</strong> In the stairwell, the flight that led down to the basement is <strong>half collapsed</strong>, and beside it the shaft opens all the way to the basement (solid black: it has no floor). <strong>Getting down to the basement:</strong> Dexterity + Athletics Diff. 2. The “Climb down” region is at the low end of the flight and leads to the foot of the basement stairs; a failure can mean the fall down the shaft. The shaft region leads to the rubble in the basement (a one-story fall, about 3 m). From the basement, the “Climb up” region brings you back to the landing at the top of the flight.</p>\n<p><strong>Off the map.</strong> The rest of the building (floors 2 through 4, burned and roofless) isn&#39;t played.</p>\n\n<p class=\"sbn-moviles\">The movable furniture (1) are unlocked tiles: they can be moved, knocked over or used as a barricade.</p>",
      "moviles": []
    }
  },
